WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.570
A coin, thrown twenty times.

2
00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:03.440
Heads.

3
00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:04.420
Tails.

4
00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:05.340
Heads.

5
00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:06.370
Heads.

6
00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:10.950
When the last throw lands, the tally
reads fifteen heads out of twenty.

7
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.410
Fair coins do have lucky streaks.

8
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:15.450
So is this one biased?

9
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.560
And how sure could you ever be?

10
00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.690
In this mission, you'll
start from a null hypothesis:

11
00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:22.240
the coin is fair.

12
00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:25.140
Then ask how unlikely
your result would be.

13
00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:28.030
You'll model the heads with
a binomial distribution:

14
00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.190
twenty throws, probability
nought point five.

15
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:34.820
You'll set a significance level,
a cut-off for too unlikely,

16
00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:36.360
such as five per cent.

17
00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:41.010
And because bias could go either way,
you'll learn when to look at both tails.

18
00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:45.560
Your mission: test the coin for
bias, and decide how sure you can be.
